It creates the bones files on the ramdisk, and is _supposed_ to copy them
to the levels directory before exiting.  It does not.  If you have a fast
hard drive, you can get around this by assigning ramdisk and levels (in
your nethack.cnf) to the same place on the HD.  I use a script that runs
hack and then copies any bones files on the ramdisk into the levels
directory.  Seems to work.
                                                         
